Author: James Cherti &#60;https://www.jamescherti.com/&#62; License: GPL The wizard Emacs package provides a collection of useful Emacs functions. The philosophy behind this package is simple: use the built-in functions Emacs already provides to do what complex third-party packages do. Instead of rewriting complex logic from scratch or adding heavy external dependencies, wizard uses built-in Emacs functions to deliver practical features. (For example, to highlighting symbols uses the built-in hi-lock) Features Overview Visuals &#38; Highlighting Symbol highlight: (wizard-toggle-highlight-at-point) toggles highlighting for the symbol under your cursor or the active selection. It is a lightweight alternative to the highlight-symbol package. Native TODO highlighting: &#8230; <a href="https://www.jamescherti.com/emacs-wizard-el/">Continue reading <span class="meta-nav">&#8594;</span></a>